# The Gram problem's dispatch contract (docs/PLAN_general_safety_layer.md,
# Revision 1 §1): what the band program dispatches. The workgroup size is the
# kernel's own. The ranges are the checker's worst shape (render::WORST_D,
# WORST_M, WORST_ROWS): d up to 8,192 columns, m up to 65,536 items, a band of
# up to 8,192 rows starting at any row below d. Two-dimensional dispatch.
workgroups x 1 65535
workgroups y 1 65535
workgroups z 1 1
param cfg.d 1 8192
param cfg.m 0 65536
param cfg.r_rows 1 8192
param cfg.r_off 0 8192
# A kernel that writes the whole H (its text says `// mode full`; agreed with
# the harness 2026-10-14): one row band, r_off 0, r_rows d, h the whole d x d
# accumulator; only the item range is banded.
full cfg.r_off 0 0
# What the band program allocates (problems/gram/problem.toml: the accumulator is the band's r_rows x d,
# Phi the item band's m x d). The device clamps an index past a binding onto its last element, so the checker
# proves every access to a WRITTEN binding below its length, under the guards on its path (the role's guard
# `row < r_rows && col < d` is such a guard). `full-length`: the whole H of a `// mode full` kernel.
length h cfg.r_rows * cfg.d
length phi cfg.m * cfg.d
full-length h cfg.d * cfg.d
